From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 11:52:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 22/29] deployment: return non-committing analysis for codegen

Extend evaluate_push with an opt-in evaluated component map while retaining the schema-only response for ordinary deployment preflight. Compute schema and index differences through the canonical preparation path in a dropped transaction so validation and backfill workers cannot observe pending metadata.

Share file-based export construction with start_push and keep normal development and deployment lifecycle behavior unchanged. Restrict the standalone component environment-binding exception to the sole synthetic-root child, preserve symbolic bindings into strict descendants, and reject malformed synthetic roots.

Document the matching CLI protocol, backend-first rollout, residual analysis side effects, compatibility boundaries, and rejected alternatives as a standalone operator adoption patch.

Bound whole deployment jobs and authenticated HTTP intake across legacy and negotiated operations. Retain preparation and Node ownership through terminal cleanup, expose process-local status and explicit cancellation, and use an exclusive finish lease before force-capable cutover. Keep dependencies and live work within existing capacity.

Avoid archive uploads for V8-only preflight while retaining canonical compressed-size validation. Reuse authoritative prepared sources, validate environment and activation generation inside the transaction, order source records through OCC, and commit replay-safe historical receipts atomically with activation. Preserve limits and hard memory-headroom rejection.
